<+>File Handler Plan (Team B)\r\n\r\nResponsibility\r\n- Own all direct file system access for data files.\r\n- Provide program control a clean API: list available files and return contents.\r\n- Keep data folder location flexible (project root /data or working‑dir /data).\r\n\r\nInputs\r\n- Requests to list files.\r\n- Requests to read a file by index or filename.\r\n\r\nOutputs\r\n- Sorted list of filenames.\r\n- Raw file contents as a String.\r\n\r\nInterface (proposed)\r\n- class FileCatalog\r\n  - List<String> listFiles()\r\n  - Optional<String> getByIndex(int index)\r\n  - Optional<String> getByName(String filename)\r\n  - String dataDir\r\n- class FileReaderService\r\n  - String readFile(String path)\r\n\r\nBehavior\r\n- Resolve data directory in this order:\r\n  1) ./data (project root)\r\n  2) ./build/../data if running from build (fallback)\r\n  3) working‑dir/data (same folder as program)\r\n- listFiles() returns sorted filenames (case‑insensitive) with 1‑based indices.\r\n- getByIndex() maps the user number to the sorted list.\r\n- readFile() returns raw file contents (no decipher here).\r\n\r\nError Handling\r\n- If data directory missing or empty: return empty list and a descriptive error.\r\n- If file cannot be read: return an error message to program control.\r\n\r\nTesting Ideas (TDD)\r\n- listFiles() on empty data dir returns empty list.\r\n- listFiles() returns sorted order and 1‑based indices.\r\n- getByIndex() with invalid index returns empty.\r\n- readFile() returns exact file contents.\r\n
